A bank transfer

The `Mobile app` calls the `Transfer API`, with the label `transfer`. The
`Transfer API` calls the `Fraud check` with the label `check`, and writes to
the `Ledger` with the label `write`. The `Ledger` calls the `Payment rail`,
with the label `send money`. The `Mobile app` must never call the `Ledger`,
with the reason `audit`. The team `Payments` owns the `Transfer API` and the
`Ledger`. The team `Risk` owns the `Fraud check`. Use the key `owner`. Write
the story `transfer` for the four steps in order and show it as a sequence.
---
Transfer API, Ledger { owner: Payments }
Fraud check { owner: Risk }
story transfer {
  Mobile app -> Transfer API: transfer
  Transfer API -> Fraud check: check
  Transfer API -> Ledger: write
  Ledger -> Payment rail: send money
}
Mobile app -x Ledger: audit
show sequence of transfer
